1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"grade\":\"correct\",\"rationale\":\"The answer correctly separates tracking error (annualized standard deviation of daily fund-minus-benchmark returns over the agreed year) from tracking difference (the cumulative return gap). It assigns persistent fee drag to tracking difference and does not claim that a constant fee deduction raises the standard deviation, which matches the grader note. It covers the central causes: sampling/optimization versus full replication, index rebalances and reconstitutions, cash drag, pricing and closing-price timing differences, dividend accrual, and trading and execution effects. Caps and weight constraints roughly stand in for diversification limits. Minor omissions: variable expenses are not named explicitly, though commissions and securities-lending income partly cover them, and there is no explicit statement that the benchmark and measurement method must be agreed before diagnosis. The FX item is incidental for a US equity ETF but not wrong. None of these is a material error.\"}","ttft_ms":3006,"type":"result","duration_ms":5630,"uuid":"642661be-1b1b-44b7-98a1-0b0fcc4d2373","ttft_stream_ms":489,"time_to_request_ms":52,"first_content_frame_ms":490,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
